---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';

const effectiveDate = 'October 12, 2026';
const email = site.contact.email;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of the Giaccio Properties website."
>
  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p>Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
      </div>

      <p>
        These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of the Giaccio Properties website. By using this
        website, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>About this website</h2>
      <p>
        This website presents a portfolio of homes across {site.contact.area}.
        Some are available, some have been sold, and some are rented. The site is informational: it lets
        you browse the homes and get in touch with us. Nothing on this website is an offer, a contract, or
        a solicitation in any place where that would be unlawful.
      </p>

      <h2>Property information is not guaranteed</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep listing details accurate, but all property information &mdash; including prices,
        availability, status, square footage, lot size, features, descriptions, and photographs &mdash; is
        provided for general information and is subject to change or withdrawal without notice. Information
        is deemed reliable but is not guaranteed and should be independently verified. Photographs and
        descriptions may be illustrative and may not reflect the current condition of a property. Nothing
        on this site constitutes an appraisal or a representation about the value or condition of any
        property.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Content on this website is not legal, financial, tax, or investment advice. Any decision to buy,
        sell, or rent a property should be made with the help of your own qualified professionals.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair Housing</h2>
      <p>
        We support the principles of equal housing opportunity. We do not discriminate on the basis of
        race, color, religion, sex, disability, familial status, national origin, or any other class
        protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to use this website only for lawful purposes. You may not attempt to disrupt or gain
        unauthorized access to the site, collect information from it through automated means without our
        permission, or use it in any way that infringes the rights of others.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this website, including text, photographs, graphics, and the Giaccio Properties
        name, is owned by or licensed to us and is protected by applicable law. You may view and share
        pages for personal, non-commercial use, but you may not copy, reproduce, or use our content for
        other purposes without our written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Links and embedded content</h2>
      <p>
        This website may link to or embed content from third parties, such as mapping services. We are not
        responsible for the content, policies, or practices of those third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available,&rdquo; without warranties of
        any kind, whether express or implied, to the fullest extent permitted by law. We do not warrant
        that the site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Giaccio Properties will not be liable for any indirect,
        incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, this website or
        the information on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we will revise the effective date above.
        Your continued use of the website means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to its conflict-of-law
        rules.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>{site.contact.address ? `, or by mail to ${site.contact.address}.` : '.'}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
